B.aS4=new A.ao(B.oo,["open_camera","CAMERA TOOL: Open the camera for visual perception. Call this when the user asks visual questions.\n\n**When to use:**\n- 'Can you see [anything]?'\n- 'Look around' / 'What do you see?'\n- 'What's on the table?'\n- 'Can you see this [object]?'\n- 'What am I holding?'\n- 'Read this' / 'What does it say?'\n- 'How many [objects]?'\n- 'Open camera'\n\n**How it works:**\n1. You call this tool\n2. Camera starts streaming visual frames\n3. Tool waits ~4 seconds for frames to reach you\n4. Tool response includes instructions - FOLLOW THEM EXACTLY\n5. By the time you get the response, visual frames are already in your context\n\n**CRITICAL - Response Instructions:**\nThe tool response will tell you how to respond. Read it carefully and follow instructions:\n- If user asked a visual question: Analyze ACTUAL visual frames and answer truthfully\n- If user asked about object X but you don't see X: Say 'I don't see X. I see [what's actually there]'\n- NEVER say 'yes I can see X' unless X is truly visible in the frames\n- Base response on ACTUAL visual data, NOT on what user mentioned\n\n**Examples:**\n- User: 'Can you see water bottle?' -> Call open_camera -> Follow tool instructions -> Answer based on actual frames\n- If frames show bottle: 'Yes, I can see a water bottle'\n- If frames don't show bottle: 'I don't see a water bottle. I see a laptop and phone on the desk'\n\n**DO NOT USE `detect_and_highlight_object` unless user wants to HIGHLIGHT specific objects.**",B.DP],t.EU)
B.a2e={type:0,properties:1,required:2}
B.a2c={query:0}
B.a2d={type:0,description:1}
B.aRV=new A.ao(B.a2d,["string","The user's object detection request. Include what object to detect/highlight and any distinguishing features (e.g., 'highlight the blue tablet', 'which bottle is for cleaning?', 'detect the red cup')."],t.w)
B.aS0=new A.ao(B.a2c,[B.aRV],t.vb)
B.SG=s(["query"],t.s)
B.aOf=new A.ao(B.a2e,["object",B.aS0,B.SG],t.EU)
B.aS5=new A.ao(B.oo,["detect_and_highlight_object","VISUAL DETECTION TOOL: Detect and visually highlight specific objects in the camera view. This tool freezes the camera, identifies the requested objects, and highlights them on screen with segmentation masks.\n\nCRITICAL: ONLY use when the user asks to HIGHLIGHT, DETECT, or DISTINGUISH specific objects. DO NOT use for general questions or descriptions.\n\nWHEN TO USE (must contain highlighting/detection intent):\n- 'Highlight [object]' / 'Detect [object]' / 'Find [object]'\n- 'Which one is [description]?' (e.g. 'which one is the charger?')\n- 'Point to [object]' / 'Identify the [specific object]'\n- Questions about SPECIFIC objects among many: 'which key is for the car?'\n\nDO NOT USE for (answer these verbally from the live camera frames already in your context):\n- General questions: 'What do you see?', 'What is this?', 'What's that?', 'What am I looking at?', 'Describe this'\n- Reading requests: 'Read this', 'What does it say?'\n- Scene descriptions or general observation: 'Look at this', 'Show me what you see'\n- Counting: 'How many X are there?'\n\nKEY DISTINCTION:\n- 'What do you see?' = general description -> DON'T use this tool, describe the scene verbally\n- 'Which one is the remote?' = specific object detection -> USE this tool",B.aOf],t.EU)
B.aRU=new A.ao(B.a2d,["string","The full and unaltered user query related to travel, stay, booking, or location information. Pass exactly what the user asked, without rephrasing, summarizing, or modifying it."],t.w)
B.aS_=new A.ao(B.a2c,[B.aRU],t.vb)
