B.aS6=new A.ao(B.oo,["location_search","CRITICAL: This function MUST be called for ANY user queries related to travel, stay, or location-based information. The model must NEVER deny or say it cannot perform the task \u2014 it must ALWAYS pass the user's full query to this function instead.\n\nThis includes ANY query involving planning, finding, comparing, recommending, checking, exploring, or BOOKING \u2014 for hotels, restaurants, weather, flights, events, directions, or itineraries.\n\nThe model should not attempt to answer, explain, or reject the user's query \u2014 only forward it entirely to this function.\n\nExamples: 'Book a hotel in Delhi', 'Find a hotel near Connaught Place', 'Plan a trip to Japan for 7 days', 'Create an itinerary for Kerala', 'Find restaurants near CST station', 'Flights from Mumbai to Goa on Friday', 'Weather in Shimla next weekend', 'Events in Bangalore this weekend', 'Directions from Pune to Lonavala', etc.",B.aOe],t.EU)
B.aS7=new A.ao(B.oo,["close_camera","CAMERA TOOL: Close the device camera when it is no longer needed. The voice call stays active.\n\n**WHEN TO USE:**\n- User asks to stop or close the camera\n- After finishing camera-based tasks to free system resources",B.DP],t.EU)
B.aS8=new A.ao(B.oo,["capture_camera_frame","CAMERA CAPTURE TOOL: Capture and save the current camera frame as an image. Use this when the user wants to take a picture or save the current view.\n\n**WHEN TO USE:**\n- User requests to capture/take a picture: 'capture this', 'take a picture', 'save this image'\n- User wants to save what the camera is currently seeing: 'save this view', 'capture the current frame'\n- User asks to take a photo: 'take a photo', 'snap a picture', 'can you capture this'\n\n**IMPORTANT: The camera (video mode) must already be open before using this tool. If it is not open, tell the user to open the camera first.**\n\n**EXAMPLES:**\n- User: 'Can you please capture this' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'Take a picture of this' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'Save this image' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'Capture the current frame' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'What do you see?' -> NOT a capture request, describe the live camera frames instead\n- User: 'Highlight the bottle' -> use detect_and_highlight_object instead",B.DP],t.EU)
